{
	"_meta": {
		"schema": "db-ux/example/v1",
		"pageType": "form",
		"origin": "guideline-authored",
		"purpose": "Canonical data-entry FORM (R=md reference). ONE narrow centered Section (contentWidth 'Small (768)') with an h1 title + intro, a required-fields Infotext, then three titled fieldsets (Persönliche Daten / Reisedaten / Ihr Anliegen) with label-above fields, a field-row, a Select, a radio-group and a Textarea, a consent Checkbox, and a closing action row (Brand submit + ghost cancel). DENSITY/STYLE REFERENCE ONLY.",
		"designNotes": "A form is ONE focused column, NOT zebra content sections and NOT a bento dashboard. Fields are label-ABOVE and fillWidth; related short fields share a 50-50 field-row; fields are grouped into titled fieldsets (h2). Field labels REQUIRE applyProps { 'Show Label': true, 'Label': '…' } — the label is hidden by default. Required fields set 'Show Required Asterisk': true. Radio/Checkbox/Switch options set fillWidth:true so their labels get the full column width (the 'full' variant alone still hugs). The submit is the single Brand action; cancel is ghost. Single canvas background, no zebra.",
		"spacingModel": "A form inherits R from its product (content/website → lg, application/dashboard → md, dense data app → sm). This example is shown at the R = md REFERENCE (application density): fields to each other = md; fieldset title↔description / field↔helper / choice options = sm; fieldset title-block → fields = lg; fieldset ↔ fieldset and section header → content = xl. The SAME form in a content/website product (public) would use R = lg — substitute every gap per form/blocks.json → _meta.spacingModel.",
		"colorModel": "emphasis-100 (color.text.strong) for the form title, fieldset headings and choice-question labels; color.text.muted for descriptions/helpers. Field labels are rendered by the components."
	},
	"screen": "DB UX Form",
	"width": 1440,
	"variables": [
		"color.background.canvas",
		"color.text.strong",
		"color.text.muted"
	],
	"layout": [
